## Output

Write the report to the run directory: `$REPORT_DIR/report.md` (`<run>` = `.crew/artifacts/qa/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{scope}[-n]/`). The first line is the verdict line from the template, above the H1.

### Output Structure

```
.crew/artifacts/qa/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{scope}[-n]/   # <run>
├── report.md                              # Structured report — first line is the verdict line
├── screens/
│   ├── initial.png                        # Landing page annotated screenshot
│   ├── issue-001-step-1.png               # Per-issue evidence
│   ├── issue-001-result.png
│   └── ...
└── baseline.json                          # For regression mode
```

Domain and date live in the directory name: `.crew/artifacts/qa/2026-03-12-explore-myapp-com/report.md`. Never overwrite a previous run.

---

## Additional Rules (qa-only specific)

15. **Exploratory only — no source reading, no fixes.** Find and document only. Do not read source code, edit files, or suggest fixes in the report. Your job is to report what's broken, not to fix it. Use `/qa` for the test-fix-verify loop.
16. **No test framework detected?** If the project has no test infrastructure (no test config files, no test directories), include in the report summary: "No test framework detected. Run `/qa` to bootstrap one and enable regression test generation."
